      "content": "but it's more than just the time. like you said, they're avoiding traffic, but they aren't even opening the pipes. they just place those black boxes, wait, and then leave. and it's always in the exact same spots near the drains, even when there's no reported leak or issue in our area. it feels like the \"maintenance\" is just a cover so they can install something underground without anyone asking questions. if someone were trying to monitor vibrations or movement from underneath the street, wouldn't they need to be active when the city is quiet? does it seem possible that this isn't actually water utility work at all?",
